+# VCF 9.1 research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14:
+
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — checked the VCF 9.1 target family and the VCF Operations, VCF Automation, and VCF Operations for Networks combination represented by the pinned compatibility snapshot.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — checked the Operations-first 9.0.x-to-9.1 sequence, the move from Fleet Management Appliance and external Identity Broker into VCF Management Services, Automation's in-place path, Fleet LCM handling for Operations for Networks, and log migration after management components.
+- **How to log into the Log Management UI in VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/442141 — checked that 9.1 Log Management is a built-in service on VCF Management Services and is surfaced through VCF Operations rather than designed as a new standalone Operations for Logs appliance.
+- **vmware/vcf-api-specs tag 9.1.0.0** — https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/tree/9.1.0.0 — checked the tagged VCF Installer `SddcSpec` contract used by the delivered installer artifact.
